abstract: >-
  PerceptFence proposes a content-layer mediation architecture for screen-share
  AI assistants and releases a deterministic synthetic-fixture reference
  scaffold. The artifact routes fixture scenario labels to fixed redaction,
  per-invocation memory-gate, output, and in-memory audit actions. Its redaction
  surface is evaluated on a self-generated deterministic coverage census and a
  seed-paired comparison with Microsoft Presidio. It does not implement live
  capture, authenticated re-consent, persistent cross-session memory, or an
  external model adapter. Synthetic-only; no real captures or personal data.
